# Project instructions

- Read `.gig/JOB.md` before working. Price and payment facts come only from `.gig/QUOTE.md`; quotes in old reports are void.
- Original materials are read-only{% if material_path %}: `{{ material_path }}`{% endif %}. Copy needed samples to `data/`; client samples are never committed.
- New results go to new directories, never overwriting old ones; failures and unusable states stay visible.
- Never tune numbers toward the client's expectations or a paper. Reported figures come from saved results, with the data split, configuration and aggregation stated.
- At the end of every phase append to "Status" in `.gig/JOB.md`: commands, verification figures, commit, remaining work, whether anything was sent out.
- Temporary files and recovery copies go in `.scratch/`, cleared at the end of a phase. Create nothing in the parent directory.
- Actions that need JC's explicit approval: sending anything out, pushing to a remote, deleting or archiving, paid remote resources, scope changes beyond the confirmed decisions, edits to `.gig/QUOTE.md`.
- ASCII punctuation in prose. English directory and file names. Explain concepts with concrete names, no undefined abbreviations.
- Reports use Kami or LaTeX; keep only the final PDF; sources in `.scratch/reports/`, prose through humanizer (humanizer-zh for Chinese).
- Commit each verified unit of work locally; pushing needs separate authorisation.

